                <pb facs="0206" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890d.00/259: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Beirut</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-17T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1925—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department has no intention at present of withdrawing destroyers in view of
                    situation set forth in your telegram of November 16, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
